<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia zinc output fell in 1996.</title>
<headline>Tunisia zinc output fell in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisian zinc output in 1996 fell to 58,000 tonnes from 80,600 tonnes in 1995, official statistics showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The fall was caused by the closure in October last year of the country's Bougrine zinc mine because of falling world prices.</p>
<p>Inmet in October shut down the northwestern Bougrine mine developed since 1994 by Toronto-based Metall Mining Corp.</p>
<p>Metall later passed the Bougrine mine to Inmet.</p>
<p>Tunisia also produced 7,700 tonnes of lead in 1996, down from 11,300 tonnes in 1995, the statistics showed.</p>
<p>Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
